# File: scripts/__tests__/sdlc-execute-gh-retry.test.mjs
# Generated from: specs/603-stop-retrying-gh-calls-whose-error-names-issue-number-502-503-or-504/requirements.md
Feature: Stop retrying gh calls whose error names issue number 502, 503 or 504

  @SCN001 @regression
  Scenario Outline: An issue number is not a transient failure
    Given a gh call that fails with "GraphQL: Could not resolve to an issue or pull request with the number of <number>. (repository.issue)"
    When the retry wrapper runs it
    Then the call runs once
    And its failure is returned without any backoff sleep

    Examples:
      | number |
      | 502    |
      | 503    |
      | 504    |

  @SCN002 @regression
  Scenario Outline: Real HTTP 5xx failures are still retried
    Given a gh call that always fails with the output "<output>"
    When the retry wrapper runs it
    Then the call runs four times with backoff sleeps of 1000, 2000 and 4000 ms

    Examples:
      | output                  |
      | HTTP 502                |
      | HTTP 503                |
      | HTTP 504                |
      | 502 Bad Gateway         |
      | 503 Service Unavailable |
      | 504 Gateway Timeout     |

  @SCN003 @regression
  Scenario Outline: Other transient signals are unchanged
    Given a gh call that always fails with <failure>
    When the retry wrapper runs it
    Then the call runs four times with backoff sleeps of 1000, 2000 and 4000 ms

    Examples:
      | failure                                              |
      | the output "request timed out"                       |
      | the output "connection reset by peer"                |
      | the output "connection refused"                      |
      | the output "could not resolve host: api.github.com"  |
      | the output "TLS handshake timeout"                   |
      | the output "unexpected EOF"                          |
      | a spawn error with code EPIPE                        |
